<title>USA: Movado Group Q2 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Movado Group Q2 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>LYNDHURST, N.J. 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>MOVADO GROUP, INC.</p>
<p>			 Consolidated Statements of Income</p>
<p>		     (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				    (Unaudited)</p>
<p>				 Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					    July 31,	  July 31,</p>
<p>				     1996     1995	1996     1995</p>
<p> Net sales		    $50,751  $43,986   $81,764  $72,190</p>
<p> Cost of sales		 23,121   20,675    36,784   33,962</p>
<p> Gross profit		  27,630   23,311    44,980   38,228</p>
<p>Selling, general &amp;</p>
<p>  administrative expenses  23,944 19,937    41,128  35,395(a)</p>
<p> Operating profit	     3,686    3,374     3,852    2,833</p>
<p> Interest			 1,281    1,303     2,123    2,281</p>
<p> Income before taxes	  2,405    2,071     1,729	552</p>
<p> Income taxes		     722	627	 519	166</p>
<p> Net income		     1,683    1,444     1,210   386(a)</p>
<p> Net income per share	  0.28     0.24	0.20  0.06(b)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		   6,007    5,993     6,007    5,997</p>
<p>(a) Includes the effect of a one-time, pretax charge of approximately $600,000 in connection with the adoption of new accounting standards relating to the amortization of advertising production costs.</p>
<p>(b) Includes the effect of a one-time, after-tax charge of $0.07 per share in connection with the adoption of new accounting standards relating to the amortization of advertising production costs.  Excluding this one-time charge, net income for the six months would have been $0.13 per share.</p>
</text>
